    "q": "What is multimodal AI and what product use case would it unlock at an entry-level PM's scope?",
    "a": "Multimodal AI processes and generates multiple content types-text, images, audio-within a single interaction. GPT-4o, Gemini, and Claude 3 are production examples today.\n\nFramework for identifying APM-scope multimodal opportunities: Find flows where users manually describe something they could simply show. Those are your highest-signal insertion points.\n\nRecommended use case: Receipt capture in expense management. Users photograph receipts; the model extracts merchant, amount, date, and category-replacing a manual entry form entirely.\n\nBefore building, validate the assumption: Pull support tickets and session recordings to confirm manual entry is the top drop-off point. Measure current form completion rate and time-on-task as baselines.\n\nPilot: Run a 50/50 A/B test-camera-first flow versus existing form-on mobile users over four weeks.\n\nSuccess metrics:\n- Form completion rate (target: +15%)\n- Time-to-submit per expense (target: -40%)\n- Extraction accuracy (target: >92% field-level)\n- 7-day retention on the feature\n\nTrade-offs to acknowledge: OCR accuracy degrades with crumpled or low-light receipts, creating trust issues. Privacy-sensitive receipt data requires clear model data-handling disclosures. Latency on image processing (~2–3s) may frustrate users expecting instant response-progressive loading states are non-negotiable.\n\nThe APM's job is scoping the pilot narrowly enough to ship in one sprint while capturing enough signal to justify broader investment.",
