    "subcategory": "product_strategy",
    "a": "Framework: Four-lens diagnostic across data, stakeholders, users, and competitive context-completed in 30 days.\n\nWeek 1 - Data audit (validate before forming opinions):\nPull 12-month cohort retention curves-flat signals a working loop, declining signals a value gap. Review support ticket categories by volume and trend. Map feature usage distribution to identify real value vs. bloat. Critically, *validate data quality first*: check if instrumentation gaps exist before trusting any metric.\n\nWeek 2 - Stakeholder interviews:\nEngineering lead, design lead, 2-3 CSMs, 2-3 sales reps. Core questions: What have users repeatedly requested that hasn't shipped? What's been tried and failed? This surfaces institutional knowledge that dashboards never show.\n\nWeek 3 - User research:\n7 interviews across three segments: power users, recently churned, and never-activated. I'm mapping jobs-to-be-done, workarounds, and competitive alternatives.\n\nWeek 4 - Synthesis + one hypothesis to test:\nI produce a health brief with: North Star metric and trajectory, top three opportunities, two urgent fires, and one specific A/B test to run within 60 days to validate the highest-priority hypothesis.\n\nSuccess metrics: 30-day retention improvement, activation rate, support ticket deflection rate, and NPS delta by segment.\n\nTrade-off I'm aware of: Moving fast risks acting on incomplete data; moving slow loses momentum and stakeholder confidence. The pilot test resolves this-it generates real signal without committing the full roadmap.",
