    "a": "[EXAMPLE TEMPLATE  . Replace with your own real story]\n\nAt the Staff/Principal level, the leverage for developing others shifts from one-on-one mentorship to systemic impact: building environments where good PM practice becomes the default rather than the exception.\n\nThree things I've done that had the most impact:\n\n1. Institutionalized a product critique practice. I ran bi-weekly 60-minute sessions where any PM could bring an in-progress product decision for structured peer feedback. The format: 10 minutes of context, 20 minutes of questions only (no solutions), 20 minutes of observations and alternatives, 10 minutes of synthesis by the PM presenting. Within three months, I observed a measurable change in how PMs wrote their briefs  . they pre-answered the questions they expected to receive, which sharpened their own thinking before the session.\n\n2. Built a PM development framework that codified levels. Before this, PM career growth was informal and inconsistent. I partnered with our Head of Product to articulate concrete behavioral expectations at each level  . not job descriptions, but observable behaviors: \"At Senior PM level, you drive alignment without escalation; at Lead PM level, you actively sponsor others' development.\" This gave PMs a clear language for their own development and gave managers a structure for developmental conversations.\n\n3. Created a \"teaching artifact\" expectation. I made it a norm for Staff PMs to document their strategic thinking  . not just decisions, but the reasoning process, the options considered, and the framework used. These documents weren't filed away; they were shared in our PM community channel as examples. Over time, the library of reasoning examples became a training resource that new and developing PMs cited explicitly in their own work.\n\nLearning: the highest-leverage development at the Staff level is environmental  . building the conditions where good practice compounds across everyone on the team, not just the people you're directly coaching.",
