    "id": "cp-meta-b1",
    "q": "Tell me about your most impactful product decision.",
    "a": "Meta wants PMs who move fast and take ownership. This question tests judgment, not just execution.\n\nStrong answer structure:\n• What was the decision (and why was it yours to make)?\n• What was at stake (user impact, revenue, strategic direction)?\n• What options did you consider and why did you choose this one?\n• What happened  . and what would you do differently?\n\nWhat makes an answer \"impactful\" at Meta:\n• Scale: affected millions of users, not just one team\n• Speed: you made the call and moved, didn't wait for consensus\n• Measurable outcome: you can cite the metric that moved\n\nMeta's culture values \"move fast with stable infra\"  . they want PMs who bias toward shipping over perfection, but who are honest about the tradeoffs they made.\n\nAvoid: decisions where you had perfect information and it was obvious. The best answers involve genuine uncertainty, a defensible rationale, and a real outcome  . even if it was messy.",
